<div class="book-title">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim</div>
<div class="halacha-title">Hilchos Netilas Yadayim L'Seudah U'Betzi'as HaPas 4</div>

<div class="lm-subtitle">
  Based on the Torah teaching <span class="verse">"Tik'u Tochachah"</span>
  <span class="source-ref">(<span class="lm-ref">Likutay Moharan II, 8</span>)</span> — see there the entire Torah teaching from beginning to end.
</div>

<div class="paragraph" style="text-align: center; font-style: italic; color: var(--section-num); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
  And the principle, in a great brevity necessary for our subject:
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  That one needs to subdue the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> <span class="heb-def">[nourishment of the body]</span>, which is the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">heel of Eisav</span>. And to strengthen the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> <span class="heb-def">[nourishment of the soul]</span>. And this is merited through drawing down the <span class="key-concept">voice of the melody and song that will be aroused in the future</span> — which is the aspect of the voice that waters the garden, through which all the awe and the fragrances grow — which are the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"Your voice I heard in the garden, and I was awed"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Genesis 3:10)</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For this voice is the aspect of <span class="verse">"a river goes out of Eden to water the garden"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Genesis 2:10)</span>, etc. And it is the aspect of <span class="verse">"The voice — the voice is the voice of Yaakov"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Genesis 27:22)</span> — which subdues the heel of the <span class="heb-term">sitra achra</span>, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and his hand was holding the <b>heel</b> of Eisav"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Genesis 25:26)</span>, etc. — see there very well.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And to merit this voice is through the <span class="key-concept">prayer in the aspect of judgment of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span></span> [the man of power] — through which one extracts from the <span class="heb-term">sitra achra</span> all the holiness and all the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> that it swallowed. And the <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> of holiness is revealed, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"For the earth shall be full of the knowledge of Hashem, as the waters cover the sea"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Isaiah 11:9)</span>. And through this, converts are made and His glory, blessed be He, is revealed. And through this, prophecy is drawn down. And through prophecy, the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> [imaginative faculty] is refined. And through the refinement of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> — through this, the primary strengthening of the holy <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>. And then one merits complete <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> in the <span class="key-concept">renewal of the world</span> [<span class="heb-term">chidush ha'olam</span>] — which is impossible to attain through <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> alone, but only through <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>. And this is the primary foundation of the holy <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> — to believe that Hashem, blessed be He, created the world <span class="heb-term">yaish mai'ayin hamuchlat</span> <span class="heb-def">[something from absolute nothing]</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And through this <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, one merits the renewal of the world of the future. And then the world will be conducted in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>. For the primary holiness of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> is through the aspect of <span class="verse">"the power of His deeds He told to His people"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Psalms 111:6)</span>, etc. — meaning, through the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, the aspect of <span class="verse">"In the beginning, G-d created the heavens"</span> etc. As Rashi explains there — that for this reason [the Torah] opened with <span class="verse">"Beraishis"</span>: because of <span class="verse">"the power of His deeds He told"</span> etc. — so that they could conquer <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  It emerges that the primary holiness of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> is through believing in the renewal of the world — that Hashem, blessed be He, created the world something from nothing, as it is written: <span class="verse">"In the beginning, G-d created"</span> etc., as mentioned above. And the primary holiness of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span> is that there His Providence, blessed be He, is revealed, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"The eyes of Hashem your G-d are constantly upon it"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Deuteronomy 11:12)</span>, etc. And in the future, when the entire world will be conducted in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">Eretz Yisrael</span>, as mentioned above — then the entire world will be conducted only through Providence alone, and nature will be completely nullified. And then the song of Providence and wonders will be aroused, etc. And this song is the aspect of the voice mentioned above that waters the garden — through which one merits the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> and one subdues the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>, in the aspect of <span class="verse">"and his hand was holding the heel of Eisav"</span> etc. — see all this there very, very well, for they are long and deep matters, deeper than the sea; there is nothing comparable to them.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 1                                       -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 1</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> before the meal. For we, the children of Israel, the holy nation — we need to sanctify our eating with great holiness, until our eating is in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"The righteous eats to satisfy his soul"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Proverbs 13:25)</span>. For this eating is from the side of Yaakov Avinu — who subdues the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>, which is the side of Eisav, the aspect of the heel of Eisav, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, before eating, one needs to purify and sanctify our hands with water — so that we should have the power through this to subdue the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> and to strengthen the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> — so that our eating should be in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> for a meal. For through the mitzvah of washing the hands with water — through this, we draw down the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> mentioned above, which emerge through the prayer of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span> mentioned above, through which one merits all the levels mentioned above — until one merits to draw down the river that goes out of Eden to water the garden, through which the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> is drawn and the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> is subdued, in the aspect of <span class="verse">"and his hand was holding the heel of Eisav."</span>
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And for this reason, we wash the <span class="key-concept">hands</span> specifically. For the primary subduing of the heel of Eisav — which is the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> — is through the hands specifically, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and his <b>hand</b> was holding the heel of Eisav."</span> "His <b>hand</b>" — specifically. For in truth, the primary subduing is through the holiness of the hands. For all the levels mentioned in the Torah teaching mentioned above are all drawn through the aspect of hands. For the primary drawing of the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> is through the prayer of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span>, as mentioned above. And the primary aspect of <span class="heb-term">ko'ach</span> [power] is in the hands, as is known, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"the power of their hands"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Job 30:2)</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For the primary power of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span> mentioned above, who prays the prayer mentioned above — the primary purpose is that he should merit all the levels mentioned above, so that he should merit to reveal the <span class="key-concept">renewal of the world</span> in the world — that all who come into the world should know and believe the truth as it is: that the world is renewed, that Hashem, blessed be He, created the world after absolute non-existence. And through this, the melody mentioned above is drawn, etc.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  It emerges that the main thing is to reveal the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, which is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"In the beginning, G-d created the heavens and the earth."</span> And all of this is the aspect of <span class="verse">"the power of His deeds He told to His people"</span> — which are the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">twenty-eight letters of the work of Creation</span> [<span class="heb-term">kach asvan d'uvda d'Beraishis</span>] — which are the twenty-eight letters in the verse <span class="verse">"Beraishis"</span>, as is known. And with them, Hashem, blessed be He, created all of creation.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And these twenty-eight letters are the aspect of the <span class="key-concept">twenty-eight joints of the hands</span> [<span class="heb-term">kach pirkin d'yadayim</span>], as is known. It emerges that through this power of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span> mentioned above — through this, the twenty-eight letters of the work of Creation are revealed, which are the aspect of the twenty-eight joints of the hands — with which Hashem, blessed be He, created the world. As it is written: <span class="verse">"My hand also laid the foundation of the earth, and My right hand spread out the heavens"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Isaiah 48:13)</span>, etc. And all of this is the aspect of the revelation of the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, etc. — through which the river that waters the garden is drawn, which is the aspect of the voice mentioned above that subdues the heel of Eisav, in the aspect of <span class="verse">"and his hand was holding"</span> etc.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore — because all of this is the aspect of <span class="key-concept">hands</span>, which are the aspect of power, the aspect of the twenty-eight letters, etc., the aspect of the twenty-eight joints of the hands, through which the renewal of the world [was accomplished], as mentioned above — therefore, in truth, this power is drawn to the aspect of the hands specifically. And through them specifically, the heel of Eisav is subdued, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">"and his <b>hand</b> was holding the heel of Eisav."</span> "His <b>hand</b>" — specifically, as mentioned above. And for this reason, we wash the hands specifically before eating. For specifically through the holiness of the hands, one can subdue the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>, which is the aspect of the heel of Eisav, in the aspect of <span class="verse">"and his hand was holding"</span> etc., as mentioned above. And then one merits that the eating should be in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> — which is the aspect of the eating of Israel, who are the seed of Yaakov, who subdues the heel of Eisav with his hands, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For the waters of the washing are the aspect of the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> — through which the river that goes out of Eden is drawn, through which one merits to subdue the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>, which is the heel of Eisav, in the aspect of <span class="verse">"and his hand was holding the heel of Eisav"</span> — as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 2                                       -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 2</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And for this reason, the water used for washing needs to be <span class="key-concept">water in which no <span class="heb-term">melachah</span> [work/labor] was done</span>. Also, the vessel needs to be complete. For all the <span class="heb-term">melachos</span> [types of work] have a hold of the <span class="heb-term">sitra achra</span> — which clings to the <span class="key-concept">thirty-nine <span class="heb-term">melachos</span></span>, in which all the types of work in the world are included. For all the thirty-nine <span class="heb-term">melachos</span> are drawn from the contamination of the serpent — through Adam HaRishon's eating from the Tree of Knowledge through the counsel of the serpent. And through this, he was cursed with: <span class="verse">"By the sweat of your brow shall you eat bread"</span>; <span class="verse">"In sorrow shall you eat of it"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Genesis 3:19, 17)</span> — from which the thirty-nine <span class="heb-term">melachos</span> are drawn, as is known.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And the primary sin of Adam HaRishon was in eating — that he ate from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil — meaning, the blemish mentioned above: he ate forbidden food, which is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>, the aspect of the heel of Eisav. For Adam HaRishon denied the fundamental [principle] — for the serpent misled him and said to him: <span class="verse">"For G-d knows that on the day you eat of it"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Genesis 3:5)</span>, etc. And our Sages, of blessed memory, said that [the serpent] told them: <span class="maxim">"From this Tree He ate and created the world"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Sanhedrin 29a)</span>. It emerges that he denied the renewal of the world — for he listened to the counsel of the serpent, which is the aspect of <span class="verse">"and the serpent was cunning"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Genesis 3:1)</span> — mentioned in the Torah teaching mentioned above. And through all of this, the heresy against the renewal of the world intensifies.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For just as through the prayer of the <span class="heb-term">ba'al ko'ach</span> — who subdues the aspect of <span class="verse">"and the serpent was cunning"</span>, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above — through this, one merits all the levels mentioned above, until one merits to reveal the true <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, through which the eating is in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, as mentioned above — so too, conversely, G-d forbid, when the aspect of <span class="verse">"and the serpent was cunning"</span> intensifies — through this, the heresies intensify, G-d forbid, and the opinions of the <span class="heb-term">apikorsim</span> who deny the renewal of the world intensify, G-d forbid, may their name and memory be erased. And then the eating is in the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> — for the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> is weakened, as mentioned above, and the heel of Eisav — which is the contamination of the serpent, which is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> — intensifies. And all of this is the aspect of the sin of Adam HaRishon, who listened to the counsel of the serpent, the aspect of <span class="verse">"and the serpent was cunning"</span> mentioned there in the <span class="heb-term">parsha</span>, and denied the fundamental [principle of] the renewal of the world, and ate from the Tree of Knowledge — which is eating of the <span class="heb-term">sitra achra</span>, forbidden eating, which is the primary <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, in truth, when Hashem, blessed be He, wanted to have mercy on him and rectify him — He drew upon him <span class="key-concept">the voice that waters the garden</span>, as it is written there in the <span class="heb-term">parsha</span>: <span class="verse">"Your voice I heard in the garden, and I was awed"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Genesis 3:10)</span>, etc. And through this, one returns and subdues the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> and strengthens the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>. And through this, the rectification of his sin in truth began. But it has still not been fully refined until <span class="heb-term">Mashiach</span> comes, as is known.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And through his sin, he caused the thirty-nine curses — through which one needs to toil in the thirty-nine <span class="heb-term">melachos</span>, which are the aspect of <span class="verse">"by the sweat of your brow"</span> etc. It emerges that all the <span class="heb-term">melachos</span> included in the thirty-nine <span class="heb-term">melachos</span> — all of them have a hold of the contamination of the serpent, which is the opposite of all the above: through which the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> intensifies, G-d forbid, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  Therefore, the water for the washing — with which one needs to sanctify and purify the hands, in order to merit <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, as mentioned above — therefore it needs to be water <span class="key-concept">in which no <span class="heb-term">melachah</span> was done</span>: so that there should be no hold of the contamination of the serpent in them. So that we can purify the hands through them — so that [the hands] should have the power to subdue the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span>, which is the contamination of the serpent, as mentioned above, and to strengthen the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span>, as mentioned above — which is the aspect of the eating of Israel, who are the children of Yaakov, etc., as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- Section 3                                       -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section-number">§ 3 — The Complete Vessel and the <i>Emunah</i> of <i>Chidush Ha'olam</i></div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, the vessel needs to be <span class="key-concept">complete</span>. For the water symbolizes the wondrous <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> that will be revealed in the future, the aspect of: <span class="verse">"And the earth will be full of the knowledge of Hashem, as the waters cover the sea."</span> And the primary <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> is to know Hashem — meaning, to know and believe that He, blessed be He, is the Sole Primordial One, He is the Former, He is the Creator [who creates] something from absolute nothing — meaning, the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, as mentioned above, and as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above. For through the <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> — the aspect of <span class="verse">"and the earth will be full of knowledge"</span> etc. — one merits the levels mentioned above, until one merits this <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>: namely, the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, which is the main thing, as mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And this <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> mentioned above — which is the aspect of water — it is impossible to attain and receive except through a <span class="key-concept">vessel</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="heb-term">emunah</span>, which is in the aspect of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> <span class="heb-def">[imaginative faculty]</span>, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above. For the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span> is the vessel of the true <span class="heb-term">da'as</span>.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  For in truth, all the opinions of the entire world — even of the great philosophers and investigators — are all merely in the power of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>. For true <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> is only to know Hashem. And this, they have not even begun to attain or taste at all. For this <span class="heb-term">da'as</span>, no one merits except exceedingly great and awesome <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span> — singular individuals of the generations. But we do not have the power to attain this <span class="heb-term">da'as</span>, and we need to strengthen ourselves only with <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> — which we merit through the refinement of the <span class="heb-term">medameh</span>, which is refined through our meriting to draw close to true <span class="heb-term">tzadikim</span>, as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
  And therefore, the vessel for <span class="heb-term">netilas yadayim</span> needs to be in completeness, without any blemish or deficiency — so that it can receive and contain the water, which is the aspect of the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> mentioned above. For when the vessel is broken and blemished, it is the aspect of: <span class="verse">"broken cisterns that cannot hold water"</span> <span class="source-ref">(Jeremiah 2:13)</span> — which is said regarding the idol-worshipping heretics who have false beliefs. Therefore, the vessel needs to be complete, in order to receive through it the waters of <span class="heb-term">da'as</span> mentioned above — through which one merits the <span class="heb-term">emunah</span> of the renewal of the world, as mentioned above, through which the primary subduing of the <span class="heb-term">mezona d'gufa</span> is accomplished and one merits <span class="heb-term">mezona d'nishmesa</span> — which is the primary intention of the washing, as mentioned above.
</div>

<!-- Translator's Summary -->
<div class="translator-summary">
  <div class="summary-heading">✦ Translator's Summary ✦</div>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    This fourth halacha, based on <strong>Likutay Moharan II, 8</strong> (<em>Tik'u Tochachah</em>), frames hand-washing as the battle between <em>mezona d'gufa</em> (body-nourishment / the heel of Eisav) and <em>mezona d'nishmesa</em> (soul-nourishment / the side of Yaakov).
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>The Core Dynamic:</strong> The voice that "waters the garden" — the song of the future — subdues the heel of Eisav. This voice is drawn through the prayer of the <em>ba'al ko'ach</em> → which reveals <em>da'as</em> → which produces converts and reveals Hashem's glory → which draws prophecy → which refines the <em>medameh</em> → which produces <em>emunah</em> in <em>chidush ha'olam</em> (renewal of the world from nothing) → which brings the future world where nature is replaced by Providence → which arouses the song → which subdues body-nourishment and elevates soul-nourishment.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>28 Letters = 28 Joints:</strong> The 28 letters of the verse <em>Beraishis bara</em> = the 28 joints of the two hands (<em>ko'ach pirkin d'yadayim</em>). The hands are the instrument through which creation occurred ("My hand laid the foundation of the earth") and through which the heel of Eisav is grasped. Therefore we wash the <em>hands</em> specifically.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-bottom:0.8rem;">
    <strong>39 Melachos:</strong> The 39 categories of forbidden Shabbos labor derive from Adam's curse — "by the sweat of your brow" — itself a consequence of eating from the Tree of Knowledge through the serpent's counsel. Therefore, water for hand-washing must not have been used for any <em>melachah</em> — to be free of the serpent's contamination.
  </p>

